id: pm-bn3ppf
title: "A key-named assignment inside a rejected reference value is never judged: the whole-value password grammar consumes a spaced command substitution, so the flat scan skips a password assignment written inside it"
description: "Found 2026-11-17 while fixing pm-hw00c2. Since the whole-value password grammar (pm-ycgb5g, merged after the 2026.11.17 cut, so not yet released), password_assignment captures a value that is a spaced command substitution whole; it spells nothing, the match is rejected, and the flat scan resumes after the match, so a password assignment written inside that command (an echo of another password key with a literal value) is never visited. The published 2026.11.17 package reports that shape (measured against the npm tarball with scanMutationSecrets), and main does not, so this is a detection regression that would ship in the next cut. The structured pass is unaffected because it judges every key on its own. Fix direction: after a rejected flat match whose value holds a reference, judge each later key inside that value once, without rescanning inside those inner matches, so each character is scanned at most twice. Duplicate check: searched password command substitution inner assignment rejected value rescan; pm-ycgb5g (closed, introduced the grammar) and pm-jcz7qz (adversarial residuals) are related, and neither owns judging keys inside a rejected value."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:sdk",credential-redaction,regression,secret-guard,security
created_at: "2026-11-17T08:43:52.133Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-17T09:26:20.656Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-17T09:05:23.580Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-17T09:05:23.580Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: "A key-named assignment written inside a rejected reference value is judged at its own key in the flat scan, for every key-named rule; The rescan runs only for a rejected match whose value holds a reference and never recurses, so the linear-time controls still pass; The published 2026.11.17 verdict for a password assignment inside a spaced command substitution is restored"
parent: pm-qwoy
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: "secret-rules.ts findSecretRuleMatches: after a rejected flat match of a rule with a literal minimum whose value holds a reference opener, keysInsideRejectedValue judges each key that starts inside that value once with a per-scan copy of the flat pattern; inner matches are never rescanned, so each character is read at most twice. Applies to password_assignment and credential_key_assignment. Documented in docs/MUTATION_INTEGRITY.md."
expected_result: "A password assignment written inside a spaced command substitution of another password value is reported in the repository scan and the SDK guard, as in 2026.11.17, and the scan stays linear"
actual_result: "The pm-bn3ppf cases pass in both consumers (inner password assignment, inner credential key after a rejected path-shaped literal, clean reference values, five pinned linear-time inputs), the security suites and pnpm quality:static pass, and the inner-assignment case fails on main 94773473b while the published 2026.11.17 tarball reports it"
component: secret-guard
