comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-17T09:26:20.656Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 1 on PR 1746 widened this fix. The rescan now triggers for every reference or placeholder opener (dollar-brace, dollar-paren, dollar-name, angle), not only command and braced references. A rejected inner value that holds a reference is entered in turn, so a password assignment two references deep, or inside a placeholder or a required-variable message, is reached. Linearity: the rescan runs only for a rule whose sole predicate is its literal minimum (password_assignment). Such a rejected value spells fewer literal characters than any key of the rule with its separator, so every key inside it sits in a reference body, and bodies nest a bounded number of levels. credential_key_assignment, which also rejects on entropy and its literal grammar, uses its baseline reading instead. Pinned linear-time rows cover nested siblings and placeholder chains."
